In Inder Mohan Goswami v. State of Uttaranchal, (2007) 12 SCC 1, ("Inder Mohan Goswami")
while dealing with Section 420 IPC, this Court observed thus:
"42.

23. As per Section 464IPC, a person is said to have made a "false document":
(i) if he has made or executed a document claiming to be someone else or authorised by someone else;
(ii) if he has altered or tampered a document;
or (iii) if he has obtained a document by practising deception, or from a person not in control of his senses.
24.
